  "answer": "The knowledge base describes the main stages of password cracking as follows:\n\n1. **Attack Description**: An adversary attempts to guess the password by trying every possible value until successful. This is known as a brute force attack, which will eventually succeed if computationally feasible, as it exhaustively goes through all possible passwords based on the defined alphabet and maximum password length.\n\n2. **Execution Flow**: Adversaries may utilize brute force techniques to access accounts when passwords are unknown or when password hashes are obtained. They systematically guess the password using a repetitive or iterative mechanism, often interacting with a service that checks the validity of the credentials.\n\n3. **Exploit**: The adversary determines the finite space of possible passwords based on the password policy and then tries all possible passwords for a known user ID until access is granted by the application or system [Source 1][Source 2][Source 3].",
